1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,997
Unbroken cork would suffocate the living tissue inside.

2
00:00:03,997 --> 00:00:14,192
So at certain points the phellogen makes something else: loose, rounded, thin walled cells with big spaces between them, called complementary cells.

3
00:00:14,192 --> 00:00:19,192
They push up and burst through the surface as a raised, lens shaped pore.

